:"fc2929"},"performed_via_github_app":null},{"id":1973029504,"node_id":"MDEyOkxhYmVsZWRFdmVudDE5NzMwMjk1MDQ=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/python/mypy/issues/events/1973029504","actor":{"login":"ilevkivskyi","id":12005495,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyMDA1NDk1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12005495?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ilevkivskyi","html_url":"https://github.com/ilevkivskyi","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ilevkivskyi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ilevkivskyi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ilevkivskyi/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ilevkivskyi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ilevkivskyi/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ilevkivskyi/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ilevkivskyi/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ilevkivskyi/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ilevkivskyi/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"event":"labeled","commit_id":null,"commit_url":null,"created_at":"2018-11-18T01:34:24Z","label":{"name":"priority-1-normal","color":"fef2c0"},"performed_via_github_app":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/python/mypy/issues/comments/479261688","html_url":"https://github.com/python/mypy/issues/5903#issuecomment-479261688","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/python/mypy/issues/5903","id":479261688,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDQ3OTI2MTY4OA==","user":{"login":"BuongiornoTexas","id":48264358,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4MjY0MzU4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/48264358?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/BuongiornoTexas","html_url":"https://github.com/BuongiornoTexas","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BuongiornoTexas/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BuongiornoTexas/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BuongiornoTexas/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BuongiornoTexas/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BuongiornoTexas/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BuongiornoTexas/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BuongiornoTexas/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BuongiornoTexas/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BuongiornoTexas/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2019-04-02T23:57:18Z","updated_at":"2019-04-02T23:57:18Z","body":"I think the following is either a symptom of the same bug or is closely related (and had me going in circles for a quite a while):\r\n\r\n```python\r\nfrom typing import Dict\r\n\r\nclass Circus:\r\n\r\n    _db_config: Dict[str, str]\r\n\r\n    @property\r\n    def input_file(self) -> str:\r\n        return self._db_config.setdefault(\"Input\", \"\")\r\n\r\n    @input_file.setter\r\n    def input_file(self, value: str) -> None:\r\n        self._db_config[\"Input\"] = value\r\n\r\n    @property\r\n    def user_id(self) -> str:\r\n        return self._db_config.setdefault(\"User\", \"\")\r\n\r\n    @user_id.setter\r\n    def user_id(self, value: str) -> None:\r\n        # the next line triggers useful side effects in my code.\r\n        self.player_profile = \"\" \r\n        self._db_config[\"User\"] = value\r\n\r\n    @property\r\n    def player_profile(self) -> str:\r\n        return self._db_config.setdefault(\"Player\", \"\")\r\n\r\n    @player_profile.setter\r\n    def player_profile(self, value: str) -> None:\r\n        self._db_config[\"Player\"] = value\r\n\r\n    def __init__(self) -> None:\r\n        self._db_config = dict()\r\n\r\n        # this looks like a non-op, but triggers side effects in my code\r\n        self.user_id = self.user_id\r\n\r\n    def sell_cheese(self) -> None:\r\n        self.input_file = 'test.xml'\r\n```\r\n\r\nSorry for the long sample, but I'm not sure which parts are important (I'm pretty  new at python).\r\n\r\nStubgen yields:\r\n\r\n```python\r\n# Stubs for song_list_creator (Python 3)\r\n#\r\n# NOTE: This dynamically typed stub was automatically generated by stubgen.\r\n\r\nfrom typing import Any, Dict\r\n\r\nclass Circus:\r\n    _db_config: Dict[str, str]\r\n    @property\r\n    def input_file(self) -> str: ...\r\n    @input_file.setter\r\n    def input_file(self, value: str) -> None: ...\r\n    @property\r\n    def user_id(self) -> str: ...\r\n    @user_id.setter\r\n    player_profile: str = ...\r\n    def user_id(self, value: str) -> None: ...\r\n    @property\r\n    def player_profile(self) -> str: ...\r\n    @player_profile.setter\r\n    def player_profile(self, value: str) -> None: ...\r\n    user_id: Any = ...\r\n    def __init__(self) -> None: ...\r\n    input_file: str = ...\r\n    def sell_cheese(self) -> None: ...\r\n```\r\n\r\nI've got no problems with instance field types (declared), and I've also declared the property types. However, stubgen goes its own way and adds new declarations for the properties player_profile, user_id and Input_file as if they were instance fields. The same behaviour occurs if I delete all of the property type declarations (which is how I found the issue).\r\n\r\nI'd offer to help resolve this, but I think I need quite a bit more experience before I could do anything useful.","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/python/mypy/issues/comments/479261688/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"BuongiornoTexas","id":48264358,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4MjY0MzU4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/48264358?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.co